\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall architecture of the proposed Trans-SAR-based despeckling model. (a) Gray components denote inherited operators; colored components denote the extensions used in this work. Four encoder skips enter learned decoder fusion. Six stage-specific Fourier residual refinement (FDR) blocks and a shared latent guidance map support reconstruction. Exact inverse mapping precedes intensity residual compensation. Shapes are $H\times W\times C$ for a normalized input $Y\in [0,1]$. (b) Masked post-adaptation freezes the encoder and updates the reconstruction modules; inference uses unmasked observations.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}}
